<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Timed rally buff granted by UMW_RallyingCry (AbilityDefs/RallyingCry.xml) to every humanlike of
       the CASTER's faction in earshot/eyeshot (see CompAbilityEffect_RallyAllies). Payload is pain
       dampening only (user pick, 2026-07-24): rallied fighters shrug off wounds and hit pain-shock far
       later — a payload that stays real when a hostile AI wielder rallies its own raid, unlike the mood
       memory it replaced (mood is inert on NPCs). painFactor 0.5 sits at go-juice's painkiller tier;
       5000t (2 in-game hours) covers an engagement without lingering, and the ability's 3-day cooldown
       keeps this an heirloom moment rather than a standing aura. isBad false so it never raises a
       health alert; everCurableByItem false so medicine can't strip it.

       StaggerDurationFactor 0.5 added 2026-07-25 (user directive), which halves the walk-it-off
       slowdown a hit inflicts: RimWorld.StaggerHandler.StaggerFor multiplies its tick count by the
       pawn's StaggerDurationFactor, so the stat is live rather than one of the inert ones. Anomaly's
       RageSpeed (an enrage hediff of exactly this shape: not-bad, painFactor plus statFactors) and
       Biotech's Unstoppable gene are vanilla's only two users and both take it to 0 for outright
       immunity; half is the proportionate read for a 2-hour buff on an ordinary human, and it keeps
       "wounds barely slow them" in the ability description literally true of both halves of the
       payload. Not subject to CLAUDE.md's control-effect budget: that governs stun/stagger effects we
       inflict on others, and this is resistance on our own side, adding nothing to the census. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>UMW_Rallied</defName>
    <label>rallied</label>
    <description>Stirred by the rallying cry of a storied weapon's bearer. For a time, wounds barely register, and a hit does little to break their stride.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Disappears">
        <disappearsAfterTicks>5000</disappearsAfterTicks> <!-- 2 in-game hours -->
        <showRemainingTime>true</showRemainingTime>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <painFactor>0.5</painFactor> <!-- go-juice's painkiller tier -->
        <statFactors>
          <StaggerDurationFactor>0.5</StaggerDurationFactor> <!-- half; vanilla's only two users take it to 0 -->
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
